Where songbirds sing and fountains play,

422
00:59:56,846 --> 01:00:04,120
So sing with me: “Allah, Allah!”

423
01:00:12,726 --> 01:00:22,160
What a meaningful thing this is.
Thanks to Allah, He made us listen to this.

424
01:00:23,206 --> 01:00:26,610
We listened to many songs,
but none of them was like this.

425
01:00:27,686 --> 01:00:28,960
-Boran.
-My Bey.

426
01:00:30,046 --> 01:00:38,200
-Tell me who spoke these words that strike our hearts.
-No one heard his voice nor saw his face, my Bey.

427
01:00:39,646 --> 01:00:43,660
They call him Lover Yunus.
One of the followers of Taptuk Emre.

428
01:00:44,893 --> 01:00:46,713
O Praise be!
Praise be!

429
01:00:48,766 --> 01:00:55,040
He spoke the words coming
out of his heart, Lover Yunus. Praise be!

430
01:00:58,486 --> 01:00:59,920
Let's go.

431
01:01:09,536 --> 01:01:15,500
Fame is a disaster, fame is a disaster. It really is.

432
01:01:19,006 --> 01:01:26,560
My Bey.
A trader wants to see you. That one.

433
01:01:32,326 --> 01:01:37,600
Let's go before we die,
before the dagger of heathens reaches us,

434
01:01:38,846 --> 01:01:42,560
Before a girl falls in love with us,
hit it Bannerless, hit it!

435
01:01:43,646 --> 01:01:51,280
-Hit! Hit! Hit!
-A Bannerless does not show mercy in the field.

436
01:01:52,446 --> 01:02:01,160
No one is braver than them.
When the swords are taken out, the field is hell.

437
01:02:02,246 --> 01:02:06,320
Before the arrow of death hits us,
hit Bannerless, hit!

438
01:02:07,446 --> 01:02:13,080
Hit! Hit! Hit! Hit! Hit!

439
01:02:14,166 --> 01:02:22,000
-Tell me now, son of Bey. What brought you here.
-I'm here for an invitation.

440
01:02:24,876 --> 01:02:29,570
The nightmare of the cruel,
the hope of the innocent...

441
01:02:31,416 --> 01:02:33,926
the glorious Bey of Kayi tribe, Osman Bey...

442
01:02:34,303 --> 01:02:37,243
invites you to be the Ghazis behind him.

443
01:02:43,406 --> 01:02:47,400
To what? To be a ghazi?

444
01:02:48,806 --> 01:02:54,120
-Don't talk nonsense, son of Bey.
-Our cause is gold.

445
01:02:55,686 --> 01:03:02,040
Our cause is coin, what will you
and your father will give us?

446
01:03:03,286 --> 01:03:10,320
Without the soul of holy war,
what's the point of having treasures?

447
01:03:11,966 --> 01:03:19,240
What's better than being a ghazi
for a valiant?

448
01:03:24,446 --> 01:03:29,470
Look at those behind me. Look at them!

449
01:03:31,943 --> 01:03:35,803
They spent their lives in dungeons.

450
01:03:37,004 --> 01:03:38,964
Half of them are fugitives...

451
01:03:41,126 --> 01:03:42,650
The rest are leftovers.

452
01:03:43,268 --> 01:03:47,188
They don't even know how many
they have killed so far.

453
01:03:50,726 --> 01:03:55,040
Tell me Atmaca,
how many people have you killed?

454
01:03:56,366 --> 01:04:03,160
If I am to count, the number would
be the dark spots in my beard.

455
01:04:04,886 --> 01:04:13,920
This is the army of leaderless.
This is the guild of Bannerless.

456
01:04:15,006 --> 01:04:20,050
Our purpose is to have treasure.

457
01:04:23,806 --> 01:04:31,590
If your goal is not the holy war,
even your swords abhor you.

458
01:04:34,886 --> 01:04:36,300
Such a pity.

459
01:04:41,006 --> 01:04:48,560
Look at the boy. His father gave him Alps and horse,

460
01:04:49,246 --> 01:04:53,800
and gave him a sword, and he despises the Bannerless!

461
01:04:56,446 --> 01:04:57,460
I...

462
01:05:01,058 --> 01:05:03,788
shed my blood for what I have.

463
01:05:05,486 --> 01:05:13,120
-What sufferings did you endure, son of Bey?
-Do you think I was born to be in a palace?

464
01:05:14,326 --> 01:05:21,160
I grew up on horse, in battlefields.
If you want to test me,

465
01:05:22,326 --> 01:05:26,210
then show me the field.

466
01:05:40,606 --> 01:05:44,320
You're a lucky man Orhan Bey.

467
01:05:45,526 --> 01:05:49,720
Caravan is in our range.

468
01:05:51,046 --> 01:05:54,980
Come on. Let's see your talent.

469
01:06:02,606 --> 01:06:03,790
Come on.

470
01:06:09,006 --> 01:06:11,040
Tell me, what's the issue?

471
01:06:13,983 --> 01:06:15,313
Osman Bey.

472
01:06:17,406 --> 01:06:21,520
-How can I tell you.
-Stop babbling, trader. Just tell me.

473
01:06:22,606 --> 01:06:31,160
Cerkutay, your man who has been missing
for a long time, I know where he is.

474
01:06:35,806 --> 01:06:42,990
Cerkutay is missing since Iznik.
If you lie, I'll cut your tongue.

475
01:06:49,526 --> 01:06:51,630
I am telling you the truth, Osman Bey.

476
01:06:56,126 --> 01:06:57,740
Stop there!

477
01:07:12,406 --> 01:07:15,700
From now on, choose your words wisely.

478
01:07:18,726 --> 01:07:22,680
Osman Bey... I am trading with Lefka.

479
01:07:23,363 --> 01:07:24,363
I heard that a Turk was captured in
Lefka from one of the commanders

480
01:07:29,546 --> 01:07:34,460
They tortured him.
They tried to make him speak.

481
01:07:38,086 --> 01:07:40,610
But he kept saying the same thing.

482
01:07:42,648 --> 01:07:45,788
"I will cut you into pieces
with my double swords!"

483
01:07:49,966 --> 01:07:54,570
My brother...
My brother...

484
01:07:57,166 --> 01:08:03,760
One day, he bit one of the commanders'
ear off when they were torturing him.

485
01:08:05,686 --> 01:08:12,570
-They stabbed him on his heart, but he didn't die.
-My valiant's heart is strong.

486
01:08:19,446 --> 01:08:25,319
-It's Cerkutay. Cerkutay..
-My Bey, let me go and take my brother.

487
01:08:26,566 --> 01:08:30,240
No... Stop. What is this then?

488
01:08:30,903 --> 01:08:34,943
-I took it from a trader,
they said it belonged to Cerkutay.

489
01:08:36,366 --> 01:08:42,720
We will take Cerkutay.
I won't leave my valiant there.

490
01:08:44,206 --> 01:08:48,350
Or else, I will destroy Lefka.

491
01:08:52,845 --> 01:08:58,693
And we were going to reward the one who
brought news from my valiant with gold.

492
01:08:58,693 --> 01:08:59,843
Give it to him.

493
01:08:59,886 --> 01:09:05,639
I didn't inform you for gold, Osman Bey.
To make a big business agreement with you...

494
01:09:06,606 --> 01:09:14,520
We will reward the one who brought news
from our beloved one for sure... Don't worry. But...

495
01:09:15,966 --> 01:09:24,460
If you are lying, then
I will cut your tongue off, know that.

496
01:09:32,606 --> 01:09:37,910
Get ready. Bayindir. Bring Cerkutay's gold.

497
01:09:44,406 --> 01:09:48,020
We will either take him by talking,
or our swords will talk.

498
01:09:48,020 --> 01:09:49,240
Yes my Bey.

499
01:09:50,126 --> 01:09:53,800
Mehmus! You will come with us too.

500
01:10:05,806 --> 01:10:12,280
-Good news, Ulgen sister! Good news!
-Stop, my daughter. Do not say it right away.

501
01:10:14,566 --> 01:10:20,160
What is good news? Malhun Hatun?

502
01:10:23,246 --> 01:10:29,840
-Is it Cerkutay?
-Cerkutay! Cerkutay Bey is alive!

503
01:10:44,286 --> 01:10:52,120
Is he?
I know he is alive! I knew it!

504
01:10:55,366 --> 01:11:02,880
-My Allah... Thanks to You, my Creator...
-Finally, Ulgen.. Finally.

505
01:11:13,326 --> 01:11:21,640
My Cerkutay... Your father is coming!
Your father is alive! My Cerkutay is alive!

506
01:11:24,006 --> 01:11:25,600
My father is coming, huh?

507
01:11:45,166 --> 01:11:49,220
Food! Food!
Give us food!

508
01:12:07,806 --> 01:12:16,480
He will come, my son... He will come.
Your father is alive, I know, Cerkutay is alive.

509
01:13:37,996 --> 01:13:40,990
Lefka Castle

510
01:13:42,368 --> 01:13:45,978
Germiyanogullari Border

511
01:13:50,566 --> 01:13:51,690
My Bey...

512
01:14:08,606 --> 01:14:10,890
Mehmus convinced Osman.

513
01:14:14,448 --> 01:14:17,158
Osman is going to his cage.

514
01:14:20,046 --> 01:14:21,660
Inform Beys.

515
01:14:30,086 --> 01:14:32,910
We drew the bow,
now it is time to shoot the arrow.

516
01:14:33,253 --> 01:14:34,823
Yes my Bey.

517
01:14:41,126 --> 01:14:46,640
Forgive me, my Bey, but..
We are walking to Lefka.

518
01:14:47,846 --> 01:14:54,080
We are just a group of men.
May Allah forbid, what if they set a trap?

519
01:14:55,366 --> 01:14:58,970
Bayindir Bey, we have been searching
for Cerkutay for a long time.

520
01:14:59,158 --> 01:15:03,228
But we haven't heard from my valiant.
We sent news everywhere.

521
01:15:03,766 --> 01:15:14,240
We checked every dungeon.
But... now we will go there, even if it is a trap.

522
01:15:16,886 --> 01:15:23,440
Who said we were not crowded?
Boran.

523
01:15:24,646 --> 01:15:27,560
My Bey... The pigeon must've arrived in Sogut.

524
01:15:28,806 --> 01:15:33,360
Our Alps in Sogut are getting
ready to follow us.

525
01:15:34,606 --> 01:15:40,350
-Alps! We will spend the night in Sogut.
-Yes my Bey.

526
01:15:43,006 --> 01:15:46,580
Come on! Come on! Go!

527
01:16:18,766 --> 01:16:19,970
He is coming.

528
01:16:33,526 --> 01:16:38,960
You will never see the Beys, you messenger.
Beys can only talk to my father.

529
01:17:34,686 --> 01:17:39,160
Take this messenger. He'll be our guest for a long time.

530
01:17:48,926 --> 01:17:51,760
-Did you catch the messengers
for the others beylics, Gokmen?

531
01:17:52,366 --> 01:17:56,150
We're holding all the ways
. We'll let nobody pass, for sure.

532
01:18:00,406 --> 01:18:05,560
Mehmet Bey, I have important news for you.

533
01:18:06,566 --> 01:18:08,080
Go ahead, Atmaca.

534
01:18:08,143 --> 01:18:14,353
Someone else would take all the gold
you have for this crucial information.

535
01:18:15,006 --> 01:18:20,360
-Speak and let me value your information.
-A soldier come to the bannerless guild today.

536
01:18:21,886 --> 01:18:24,390
Orhan, son of Osman.

537
01:18:29,766 --> 01:18:32,800
He wanted to take The Bannerless beside him.

538
01:18:42,366 --> 01:18:45,880
-What did The Bannerless say?
-They haven't said anything yet.

539
01:18:47,606 --> 01:18:53,160
A caravan is coming from Constantinople.
They'll attack it together.

540
01:18:55,006 --> 01:18:57,760
After that, they will decide.

541
01:19:02,886 --> 01:19:05,520
You gave me valuable information.

542
01:19:09,486 --> 01:19:12,400
Your value is rising day by day, Atmaca.

543
01:19:22,726 --> 01:19:24,420
Gokmen!

544
01:19:27,343 --> 01:19:28,343
My Shahzade(Prince).

545
01:19:28,486 --> 01:19:32,560
Let's go and spoil Orhan's plan.

546
01:19:33,726 --> 01:19:37,120
Alps, let's go!

547
01:20:16,646 --> 01:20:19,270
Alps, let's go!

548
01:21:31,766 --> 01:21:33,800
Surround it!

549
01:23:01,006 --> 01:23:04,160
Save the princess!
Save the princess!

550
01:25:08,206 --> 01:25:09,520
Holofira.

551
01:25:14,606 --> 01:25:15,920
Orhan.

552
01:25:20,286 --> 01:25:22,200
What are you doing here?

553
01:25:47,206 --> 01:25:51,200
You've proved to be tough, son of Bey!
You are skilled.

554
01:25:53,686 --> 01:26:00,640
Wow! Wow!
Orhan Bey caught a pretty prey!

555
01:26:30,006 --> 01:26:32,490
What are they doing here?

556
01:26:43,086 --> 01:26:46,640
My Shahzade(Prince),
Germiyanids came here before us.

557
01:26:48,006 --> 01:26:51,460
Our mission will be harder than we thought.
Be cautious.

558
01:26:51,460 --> 01:26:52,460
Sure.

559
01:27:04,646 --> 01:27:06,530
Alaaddin Bey, son of Osman Bey.

560
01:27:09,686 --> 01:27:14,540
-I'm here to see Mighty Sultan.
I'm Gonca Hatun, daughter of Germiyanoglu Yakup Bey

561
01:27:15,606 --> 01:27:19,040
We're supposed to see Mighty Sultan first.

562
01:27:22,366 --> 01:27:30,480
Mighty Vizier gave strict orders.
We'll let nobody see Sultan Mesud for his safety.

563
01:27:37,446 --> 01:27:44,320
Mighty Sultan invited us personally.
This is his letter.

564
01:28:07,526 --> 01:28:16,160
Healers are with our Sultan right now, Alaaddin Bey.
We'll host you until Sultan Mesud is available.

565
01:28:31,646 --> 01:28:35,360
Let me take you to your room, Gonca Hatun.

566
01:28:49,526 --> 01:28:53,680
You'll take me to Sultan Mesud's chamber
when the dark falls.

567
01:29:03,406 --> 01:29:05,720
Stay back, Beys.

568
01:29:09,846 --> 01:29:11,560
This hatun is mine.

569
01:29:14,806 --> 01:29:18,880
You wanted to see how I fight
and you saw it.

570
01:29:20,046 --> 01:29:25,800
We believed in your war skills,
son of Bey. Eyvallah(Alright) but...

571
01:29:27,206 --> 01:29:30,080
Both the hostages and bounties are ours.

572
01:29:32,566 --> 01:29:38,960
-You are just a guest here.
-I and this hatun have a history.

573
01:29:42,886 --> 01:29:47,280
-I want no words against this!
-She won't be harmed.

574
01:29:48,486 --> 01:29:53,240
We'll send a message to her house and
deliver her safely when we get the gold.

575
01:29:56,646 --> 01:30:05,000
Don't act against our law.
If you bring the gold, you get the hatun.

576
01:30:07,126 --> 01:30:10,840
I want no words anymore!

577
01:30:12,206 --> 01:30:16,720
My Shahzade(Prince),
we will fight to the end.

578
01:30:19,726 --> 01:30:24,160
We came here to take The Bannerless
on our side, not to break them.

579
01:30:26,006 --> 01:30:34,400
Our mission is clear. We can't open another
front to fight while there is chaos in our lands.

580
01:30:41,166 --> 01:30:45,600
She won't be harmed even slightly.

581
01:30:55,366 --> 01:30:58,240
She won't be! Tie her up!

582
01:31:03,086 --> 01:31:05,520
You won't touch her!

583
01:31:30,766 --> 01:31:34,840
I thought you were a Bey.
But it seems you are a ravager.

584
01:31:39,006 --> 01:31:44,400
When we get out of here safely,
I'll tell you everything, daughter of Lord.

585
01:31:46,086 --> 01:31:51,320
-You won't leave me alone with these, right?
-I'll come back for you, Holofira.

586
01:31:56,006 --> 01:32:00,520
-Be patient.
-Don't leave me here.

587
01:32:02,486 --> 01:32:06,040
I'm talking to you, Orhan. Don't you leave me here!

588
01:32:09,726 --> 01:32:12,520
Don't be afraid. Come on.

589
01:32:41,926 --> 01:32:45,520
Dark Ali! Go to Yenisehir quickly.

590
01:32:46,566 --> 01:32:49,960
-Bring a chest of gold from my share.
-As you order, my Shahzade.

591
01:32:58,446 --> 01:33:00,680
Come on!

592
01:33:20,606 --> 01:33:23,920
We dreamed about this day a lot within
the cold walls of the monastery.

593
01:33:25,446 --> 01:33:27,600
If you want peace,

594
01:33:30,686 --> 01:33:32,440
..prepare for the war.

595
01:33:38,446 --> 01:33:42,560
We'll set the fire of riot among them!

596
01:33:46,766 --> 01:33:51,040
-Tell me about Karacahisar.
-Christian people are uneasy in Karacahisar.

597
01:33:52,246 --> 01:33:55,040
The sparks of riot are about to turn into a fire.

598
01:33:58,606 --> 01:34:03,600
-Tell me about Sogut.
-Merchants in Sogut are uneasy.

599
01:34:04,286 --> 01:34:07,360
The fire of riot will burn over them.

600
01:34:11,046 --> 01:34:17,030
The wind to grow the fire is Sultan Mesud
that I personally poisoned!

601
01:34:18,313 --> 01:34:20,393
I sent the message to Osman.

602
01:34:24,166 --> 01:34:30,720
You shot the Kayi arrow to Yakup.

603
01:34:32,166 --> 01:34:39,120
They will fight each other.
The fire will grow bigger and be their disaster!

604
01:34:40,526 --> 01:34:46,800
As we burn them,
each Christian will take courage!

605
01:34:48,926 --> 01:34:54,680
-For Christ!
-For Christ! For Christ! For Christ!

606
01:34:57,206 --> 01:35:04,880
Increase your numbers in the cities and castles!
Reach everyone! Find trustworthy men!

607
01:35:06,726 --> 01:35:12,230
Sow the seeds of riot in Christian hearts!
When Turks fight each other,

608
01:35:13,006 --> 01:35:18,000
...we'll start the riot in tribes,
citadels and cities!

609
01:35:22,886 --> 01:35:27,640
Be ready. Here we go.

610
01:35:52,686 --> 01:35:53,690
Bala.

611
01:35:58,846 --> 01:36:02,640
Bala. Bala.

612
01:36:15,566 --> 01:36:17,360
Bala.

613
01:36:23,286 --> 01:36:28,840
Bala! Bala! My Bala!

614
01:36:31,566 --> 01:36:32,850
My Bala..

615
01:36:37,846 --> 01:36:42,640
Osman!
Osman what are you doing? Go, go away!

616
01:36:43,846 --> 01:36:45,660
Go! Go! -I won't go!

617
01:36:46,046 --> 01:36:47,410
Go, it will pass on!
-No, I won't go.

618
01:36:47,886 --> 01:36:49,900
Osman, I will pass on the disease!
-I won't go anywhere, Bala!

619
01:36:50,206 --> 01:36:51,080
Go! -Don't!

620
01:37:07,686 --> 01:37:10,000
Bala...

621
01:37:11,726 --> 01:37:13,990
-Osman...
-My Halime...

622
01:37:22,486 --> 01:37:25,010
My heart's fire..

623
01:37:31,406 --> 01:37:32,660
My Halime...

624
01:37:40,126 --> 01:37:42,030
Halime..

625
01:37:45,246 --> 01:37:48,740
This wound will never heal, Osman.

626
01:37:54,166 --> 01:37:55,880
Never.

627
01:37:57,446 --> 01:38:01,240
Of course it won't close up...

628
01:38:03,606 --> 01:38:11,200
...but we will get used to it.
We will get used to it, my Bala. We will.

629
01:38:15,326 --> 01:38:22,000
But I think you seem alright.
You seem better. You are alright, right?

630
01:38:24,046 --> 01:38:28,440
I am. I am alright.

631
01:38:30,686 --> 01:38:35,120
But you don't seem alright, my Osman.

632
01:38:38,006 --> 01:38:46,720
No... I am alright. I am.
Besides, I have good news for you.

633
01:38:48,606 --> 01:38:55,320
It's not enough but it'll feel better. Cerkutay..
You know, we hadn't heard from him for a while..

634
01:38:56,606 --> 01:38:59,440
We've heard from him.
We had been looking for him.

635
01:39:00,526 --> 01:39:04,200
We heard that he was in Lefka.
Now we will go to save my valiant.

636
01:39:06,166 --> 01:39:10,680
Thanks to Allah... Thanks to Allah, my Osman.

637
01:39:12,046 --> 01:39:19,680
May Allah let him come together with his child.
May his child come together with him.

638
01:39:42,166 --> 01:39:46,960
Now tell me.
Now I am waiting for your good news!

639
01:39:48,326 --> 01:39:55,800
Tell me. The cure Alaeddin brought from India...
It helped you, right?

640
01:39:57,046 --> 01:39:58,600
-It did.
-It did.

641
01:39:59,726 --> 01:40:03,760
It works. I am feeling better than before,
don't worry.

642
01:40:04,926 --> 01:40:10,920
You are telling me the good news,
but you are hiding the bad ones, my Osman.

643
01:40:13,686 --> 01:40:19,600
I heard about Sultan Mesud.
There will be a fight, right?

644
01:40:20,766 --> 01:40:26,070
There is always a fight, my Bala.
We are trying to stop the fight.

645
01:40:26,070 --> 01:40:28,550
Don't worry about this. Don't.

646
01:40:40,766 --> 01:40:44,770
Bala... Are you alright? Huh?

647
01:40:50,446 --> 01:40:52,560
Go out! -Are you feeling alright?

648
01:40:53,726 --> 01:40:55,940
Go, Osman! Go away! -Let me give you some water.

649
01:40:58,126 --> 01:41:00,000
Here, here, drink some water.

650
01:41:01,806 --> 01:41:07,010
Drink this water.
Hatuns! Kismet Hatun! Come and see her!

651
01:41:16,526 --> 01:41:17,440
Bala..

652
01:41:21,526 --> 01:41:24,080
Drink it, drink! May it heal you.

653
01:41:31,206 --> 01:41:32,600
-Get out, Osman.
-Bala..

654
01:41:34,126 --> 01:41:35,560
-Go. Get out Osman!
-My Bala!

655
01:41:36,766 --> 01:41:37,840
-Go!
-I won't go, my Bala!

656
01:41:38,926 --> 01:41:39,760
Go, Osman!

657
01:41:41,886 --> 01:41:43,320
What is that?

658
01:41:46,286 --> 01:41:47,320
What is that?

659
01:42:02,206 --> 01:42:04,920
You said you were better...

660
01:42:06,486 --> 01:42:10,200
-You said you were better..
-I am.

661
01:42:13,646 --> 01:42:15,760
My Bala, what is this?

662
01:42:17,646 --> 01:42:19,080
Tell me!

663
01:42:23,606 --> 01:42:26,280
What is this?

664
01:42:27,406 --> 01:42:29,800
It's better than before. I am alright.

665
01:42:30,886 --> 01:42:32,400
Don't worry about me.

666
01:42:57,766 --> 01:42:59,920
Pour it here.

667
01:43:09,886 --> 01:43:13,560
If you don't want to sleep,
cover your nose and mouth.

668
01:43:15,966 --> 01:43:18,040
Come on!

669
01:43:35,326 --> 01:43:38,480
In the name of Allah...
We cannot oppose to our Bey's order.

670
01:43:39,766 --> 01:43:44,440
We will do as Osman Bey orders. Baysungur...

671
01:43:45,646 --> 01:43:47,920
Soldier disguise.
-Yes my Shahzade.

672
01:44:00,966 --> 01:44:03,800
No one can stop me from doing my duty.

673
01:44:10,446 --> 01:44:16,240
If they put something in my way,
it is my duty to get rid of it.

674
01:44:19,646 --> 01:44:23,800
They say he fights in the morning,
studies during the night.

675
01:44:28,806 --> 01:44:31,280
So Alaeddin is a scholar, huh?

676
01:44:32,366 --> 01:44:36,480
They say Osman Bey values his opinions
although he is the little brother.

677
01:44:39,086 --> 01:44:42,120
They say his intelligence is
his most cruel weapon.

678
01:44:51,846 --> 01:44:54,600
We will see whose sword is more cruel.

679
01:45:06,326 --> 01:45:08,720
Can I come in, Gonca Hatun?

680
01:45:26,406 --> 01:45:28,920
Come in.

681
01:45:38,166 --> 01:45:41,200
Guardians will switch after healers leave.

682
01:45:42,406 --> 01:45:45,320
Then I will take you to our Sultan,
Gonca Hatun.

683
01:45:48,366 --> 01:45:50,880
What about Osman's son? Alaeddin?

684
01:45:52,046 --> 01:45:55,400
-We cannot let him see the Sultan.
-He won't be able to see the Sultan.

685
01:45:56,526 --> 01:45:59,760
Now he is in his room.
Soldiers are waiting at his door.

686
01:46:01,006 --> 01:46:04,880
When the sun rises, we will send him
with empty hands.

687
01:46:33,326 --> 01:46:36,480
The scholar man who you said was intelligent
turned out to be stupid.

688
01:46:37,846 --> 01:46:39,840
Let him wait.

689
01:47:01,166 --> 01:47:08,160
Resist, Holofira...
Resist. Be patient.

690
01:47:10,166 --> 01:47:11,840
Turahan Alp.

691
01:47:13,526 --> 01:47:18,920
-When Dark Ali brings the gold, we will set out.
-Yes, my Shahzade(Prince).

692
01:47:50,846 --> 01:47:53,720
The bulgur in stew is ready, Orhan Bey.

693
01:47:56,086 --> 01:47:58,480
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

694
01:48:23,446 --> 01:48:25,200
It's so delicious.

695
01:48:26,326 --> 01:48:29,240
Come on brave boys, take a seat.

696
01:48:36,966 --> 01:48:39,880
Why would you turn halal into haram,
Mehmed Bey?

697
01:48:41,286 --> 01:48:45,280
We would share our food
if you asked.

698
01:48:46,446 --> 01:48:51,840
Only the incapable ones ask for something,
Orhan Bey. We take what we want without asking.

699
01:49:00,326 --> 01:49:02,720
Today, it's just bulgur stew.

700
01:49:04,286 --> 01:49:09,560
What will you want in the future?
Let us know so we can hide it.

701
01:49:11,606 --> 01:49:15,640
What do you even have?
Two castles and two tribes.

702
01:49:16,766 --> 01:49:20,280
What you have is like a gift
we give to our sergeants.

703
01:49:24,726 --> 01:49:28,720
Innkeeper!
Bring ayran to Mehmed Bey.

704
01:49:29,926 --> 01:49:36,320
It seems our conquests made him dry.
Let him cool off.

705
01:49:42,766 --> 01:49:44,920
We do not set eyes on them.

706
01:49:46,166 --> 01:49:49,040
We always be happy with
the victories of our minors.

707
01:49:50,246 --> 01:49:54,560
The purpose of our struggle
is not to be great.

708
01:50:01,326 --> 01:50:05,400
Our every move is for the holy war.

709
01:50:08,726 --> 01:50:11,840
But since you are happy about it,

710
01:50:14,126 --> 01:50:17,440
we will make you even more happier.

711
01:50:39,006 --> 01:50:44,160
Welcome Mehmed Bey
in a way that is worthy of his might.

712
01:50:50,806 --> 01:50:52,920
Orhan Bey!

713
01:50:58,766 --> 01:51:01,200
We'll see each other again.

714
01:51:18,086 --> 01:51:21,440
I know very well why the gold is here.

715
01:51:23,166 --> 01:51:27,800
You will see the might when the sun rises.

716
01:51:44,126 --> 01:51:48,160
Follow me Gonca Hatun,
I'll take you inside through the hidden door.

717
01:53:39,886 --> 01:53:42,000
What's this, brother?

718
01:54:18,566 --> 01:54:20,680
In the name of Allah...

719
01:54:37,606 --> 01:54:40,160
Sultan Mesud.

720
01:54:51,366 --> 01:54:53,040
My Sultan.

721
01:55:22,046 --> 01:55:25,520
My Osman Bey is deeply sad
due to your situation.

722
01:55:26,526 --> 01:55:27,840
We set out as soon as we heard about it.

723
01:55:30,086 --> 01:55:35,840
-I'm at your command. I'll do whatever
it takes for you to heal... -I've been...

724
01:55:37,326 --> 01:55:41,870
...dead for a long time.

725
01:55:42,566 --> 01:55:46,570
-My Sultan.
-Get closer. Closer.

726
01:55:50,966 --> 01:55:55,160
Inside of the pillow,

727
01:55:57,646 --> 01:56:02,680
there is a map. Take that map.

728
01:56:53,646 --> 01:56:57,400
What's this map for, my Sultan?

729
01:57:00,486 --> 01:57:02,920
The treasure.

730
01:57:05,166 --> 01:57:09,360
The treasure of Seljuks.

731
01:57:10,366 --> 01:57:13,080
I've been piling it up outside for a long time.

732
01:57:17,006 --> 01:57:21,820
Now it belongs to Osman Bey.

733
01:57:44,686 --> 01:57:49,240
Water. Water.

734
01:57:50,886 --> 01:57:53,280
Alaeddin Bey.

735
01:58:10,806 --> 01:58:12,680
My Sultan.

736
01:59:16,886 --> 01:59:21,600
Give your earnings to the needy's call,

737
01:59:22,806 --> 01:59:28,440
No matter how long you live,
death awaits us all.

738
01:59:29,846 --> 01:59:35,760
For those who see the path unfolds,

739
01:59:37,886 --> 01:59:44,120
I have mercy for the ants, and all the souls.

740
01:59:46,846 --> 01:59:49,240
Are you hungry?

741
01:59:51,846 --> 01:59:54,440
You are hungry.

742
02:00:02,046 --> 02:00:05,080
If my ancestor is Hadrat Suleyman,

743
02:00:06,166 --> 02:00:10,960
The ant that asked for a wheat
from him is your ancestor.

744
02:00:12,846 --> 02:00:16,120
It means your food is in my bag.

745
02:00:21,206 --> 02:00:23,720
They belong to others.

746
02:00:26,846 --> 02:00:33,000
The One Who crossed our paths
will take what's in my bag to you.

747
02:00:41,606 --> 02:00:43,960
He will for sure.

748
02:01:05,326 --> 02:01:11,360
Those who look but cannot see are coming.

749
02:01:24,046 --> 02:01:32,240
Dervish Effendi, what are you standing on the path.
Don't you see that we are in a hurry?

750
02:01:33,566 --> 02:01:40,880
Everyone walks towards their destinations.
It is the same for you and for these creatures.

751
02:01:44,326 --> 02:01:46,720
Dervish Effendi.

752
02:01:51,326 --> 02:01:56,240
Boran. Hold on.

753
02:02:12,846 --> 02:02:18,360
Dervish Effendi.
What lives are you talking about?

754
02:02:19,566 --> 02:02:24,720
Not me. The Righteous mentions in Holy Quran.

755
02:02:26,486 --> 02:02:32,040
He says
"O ants! Go quickly into your homes,

756
02:02:33,166 --> 02:02:37,680
so Solomon and his armies do not crush you,
unknowingly." [Surah An-Naml - 27:18]

757
02:02:46,886 --> 02:02:51,920
The Righteous protects His living beings
even from Hadrat Suleyman.

758
02:02:53,006 --> 02:03:00,200
Protect the ants, Bey.
Let them reach their destinations.

759
02:03:07,486 --> 02:03:10,480
You are so right, Dervish effendi.

760
02:03:11,726 --> 02:03:14,400
This path belongs to the ants.

761
02:03:17,326 --> 02:03:22,720
-Thank you. You showed us the right thing to do.
-Astagfirullah.

762
02:03:29,206 --> 02:03:37,400
Alps. We'll go this way.
Let's not be unfair to the ants.

763
02:03:42,846 --> 02:03:43,560
Okay my Bey.

764
02:04:00,166 --> 02:04:04,480
The one who sees what we don't see,
the one who shows it to us...

765
02:04:05,966 --> 02:04:08,200
Tell us your name Dervish Efendi.

766
02:04:10,526 --> 02:04:15,640
We escape from our name,
but you question us about what we escape.

767
02:04:18,206 --> 02:04:22,040
Just assume this poor man
is a helpless Dervish.

768
02:04:24,086 --> 02:04:26,960
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

769
02:04:32,006 --> 02:04:33,960
Come on! Go!

770
02:04:46,246 --> 02:04:49,120
And you are running
to the thing you should escape.

771
02:04:51,126 --> 02:04:52,520
Come on!

772
02:05:01,206 --> 02:05:06,600
A way with a far range who shall arrive?

773
02:05:08,166 --> 02:05:12,080
A way with countless troubles, who shall achieve?

774
02:05:14,166 --> 02:05:19,120
Preparation for the journey is needed,
it needs a little and it needs more...

775
02:05:20,326 --> 02:05:24,520
It takes an iron heart to enter this steep path.

776
02:05:25,606 --> 02:05:29,280
There are many
who can deceive others on this path...

777
02:05:30,486 --> 02:05:33,800
The disgrace of those
who follow their nafs will never go away.

778
02:05:34,926 --> 02:05:38,830
Know that there are seventy thousand soldiers
who fight for appearance on this path...

779
02:05:39,566 --> 02:05:44,170
Only a man who killed his nafs can
defeat those soldiers with his wrath...

780
02:05:46,406 --> 02:05:50,320
My father will be very happy
after he finds out that we succeeded.

781
02:06:09,686 --> 02:06:17,120
Sultan Mesud closed his worldly eyes
and opened his eyes on the other side!

782
02:06:18,646 --> 02:06:25,080
Sultan Mesud closed his worldly
eyes and opened his eyes on the other side!

783
02:06:49,206 --> 02:06:52,920
Attention! The Protector of all Turks...

784
02:06:54,006 --> 02:06:59,680
...the protector of the poor,
the enemy of the cruel, the provider of justice...

785
02:07:00,806 --> 02:07:06,640
...the Sultan of Anatolia and nearby cities,
Germiyanogullari Bey, Yakup Bey!

786
02:07:07,766 --> 02:07:10,960
What Sultan?
Where did this come from?

787
02:07:12,606 --> 02:07:16,160
Now we'll see why we are here.

788
02:07:17,806 --> 02:07:21,920
- Peace be upon you.
- Peace be upon you too.

789
02:08:02,846 --> 02:08:10,360
You must be wondering
why Yakup Bey gathered you.

790
02:08:12,406 --> 02:08:17,720
We are, Yakup Bey.
But we are more wondering what your aide said.

791
02:08:20,646 --> 02:08:26,480
We seek the good in every evil Mubarizeddin,
son of Esref.

792
02:08:35,966 --> 02:08:42,120
I got the message about Sultan Mesud.
He's in his deathbed.

793
02:08:45,406 --> 02:08:50,240
The sun of state is sinking in Konya.

794
02:08:51,926 --> 02:08:57,040
Our land is about to surrender
to a dark night.

795
02:08:58,406 --> 02:09:01,600
Terrible. Terrible.

796
02:09:03,046 --> 02:09:05,280
The sun will rise for the enemy, huh?

797
02:09:06,326 --> 02:09:11,280
Neither the sun will for the enemy
nor will our sun of state sink!

798
02:09:15,806 --> 02:09:20,640
Beys, we are here for this reason.

799
02:09:22,926 --> 02:09:25,160
As Konya surrendered to Mongolians,

800
02:09:27,006 --> 02:09:31,720
...Sultan of Turks will be one the beys of Anatolia!

801
02:09:35,686 --> 02:09:37,720
Who will lead?

802
02:09:39,846 --> 02:09:42,160
That's why I got called myself Sultan!

803
02:09:46,126 --> 02:09:49,520
I put myself in to lead the homeland.

804
02:09:50,886 --> 02:09:54,000
These lands won't remain without a head!

805
02:10:01,526 --> 02:10:04,880
Now I'm asking you, the great beys of Turkmen!

806
02:10:14,806 --> 02:10:20,240
Are you with me in my decision?

807
02:10:24,726 --> 02:10:27,840
We are, we will.

808
02:10:29,246 --> 02:10:32,320
-We're with you, Yakup Bey.
-We are with you, Yakup Bey.

809
02:10:33,446 --> 02:10:35,320
We're with you, Yakup Bey.

810
02:10:44,366 --> 02:10:46,800
The messenger must have left, my Bey.

811
02:10:49,886 --> 02:10:54,440
-Come on then. We should leave too.
-Okay.

812
02:11:01,326 --> 02:11:05,560
The seal has been impressed.
The firman must be on the way.

813
02:11:07,406 --> 02:11:12,080
When the firman arrives,
all the beys will kiss my hand.

814
02:11:13,406 --> 02:11:17,200
But him first.

815
02:11:38,086 --> 02:11:40,280
Guard! Tell your Lord...

816
02:11:41,646 --> 02:11:46,640
Osman Bey, Great Bey of Kayi,
Protector of all Turkmen, is here. Come on!

817
02:11:56,366 --> 02:12:01,720
If you want to take the hostage,
you have to leave your swords, bows and horses!

818
02:12:03,006 --> 02:12:04,880
We will never leave our horses!

819
02:12:07,486 --> 02:12:11,840
-Leave the bows and horses.
-As my Bey orders. Come on.

820
02:12:20,606 --> 02:12:22,880
Open the gate!

821
02:13:14,126 --> 02:13:18,600
-Lord Zenon.
-To what do we owe this visit, Osman Bey?

822
02:13:20,806 --> 02:13:24,680
They say you're holding
my warrior Cerkutay.

823
02:13:27,206 --> 02:13:29,600
I'll give you as much gold as you want.

824
02:13:31,646 --> 02:13:36,680
Now give me Cerkutay nicely.
Bring the gold.

825
02:13:44,486 --> 02:13:47,880
Here is the gold for my warrior.

826
02:13:50,246 --> 02:13:54,600
I don't want to shed blood.
Bring Cerkutay.

827
02:13:55,966 --> 02:13:57,840
Bring him.

828
02:14:15,246 --> 02:14:20,200
Cerkutay. Cerkutay.

829
02:14:23,286 --> 02:14:25,080
Cerkutay.

830
02:14:26,886 --> 02:14:31,640
-Cerkutay!
-Cerkutay, my brother.

831
02:14:33,806 --> 02:14:37,080
-He's alive.
-Thanks to Allah, my Bey.

832
02:14:38,286 --> 02:14:41,200
I will get you out of here.
I will get you out.

833
02:14:44,846 --> 02:14:51,400
It's enough! Your man will stay here
and you will die here. Soldiers!

834
02:14:55,366 --> 02:14:58,520
-My Bey! My Bey!
-Cerkutay! Cerkutay!

835
02:14:59,846 --> 02:15:02,960
-Protect the Bey! My Bey!
-Cerkutay!

836
02:15:04,086 --> 02:15:07,840
-Cerkutay! Cerkutay!
-My Bey! My Bey!

837
02:15:10,846 --> 02:15:12,080
Cerkutay!

838
02:15:14,686 --> 02:15:17,960
You... You... Mehmus

839
02:15:34,206 --> 02:15:39,200
So what now? Son of Bey
didn't come to take you, huh?

840
02:15:41,446 --> 02:15:47,760
I'll punish that son of Bey and you!
Greedy animals!

841
02:15:50,166 --> 02:15:54,200
I'll choke you with that gold you want!

842
02:15:55,366 --> 02:15:58,260
This woman turned out to be
a crazy one, brother.

843
02:16:02,286 --> 02:16:04,640
Someone's coming!

844
02:16:17,446 --> 02:16:22,080
-Peace be upon you
-Orhan Bey!

845
02:16:23,206 --> 02:16:27,360
I guess your horse is lame!
You came pretty quick(!)

846
02:16:32,486 --> 02:16:34,520
Dark Ali.

847
02:16:40,686 --> 02:16:44,840
It's better to keep it short,
the gold is here.

848
02:16:46,165 --> 02:16:49,879
I want the Hatun!
-Look what he says. He "wants the Hatun"

849
02:16:51,084 --> 02:16:54,959
As if he is not the one
who attacked my caravan. Marauder.

850
02:17:00,566 --> 02:17:06,000
Do you think we would give the
Hatun to you with so little gold, son of Bey?

851
02:17:08,126 --> 02:17:12,520
Who do you think you're giving?
I'm not a slave!

852
02:17:13,606 --> 02:17:16,440
I'll make you all pay for this.

853
02:17:25,366 --> 02:17:31,920
You came all the way here for nothing.
Someone else took her before you.

854
02:17:36,206 --> 02:17:41,959
Do you hear what you say Beys?
She is mine!

855
02:17:44,325 --> 02:17:46,600
I won't give her to anyone.

856
02:17:49,245 --> 02:17:52,320
Orhan Bey.

857
02:17:55,206 --> 02:17:58,080
What did I tell you?

858
02:18:01,846 --> 02:18:07,879
I take what I want without telling it.
I took her.

859
02:18:13,226 --> 02:18:14,680
This Hatun...

860
02:18:18,783 --> 02:18:20,103
is now mine.

861
02:18:23,886 --> 02:18:27,639
Lord! It was a trap, is that so?

862
02:18:33,406 --> 02:18:35,390
Come on!

863
02:19:52,726 --> 02:19:54,000
My Alps.

864
02:19:58,086 --> 02:20:00,880
My valiants.

865
02:20:02,966 --> 02:20:04,800
Drop your sword and surrender, Osman.

866
02:20:05,886 --> 02:20:09,840
Otherwise I'll throw
the heads of your alps to you.

867
02:20:11,606 --> 02:20:16,240
We do not have any soldier
behind us that are afraid to die!

868
02:20:17,326 --> 02:20:21,040
Come on, Lord! Come on!

869
02:20:37,996 --> 02:20:39,710
Osman Bey.

870
02:20:42,086 --> 02:20:47,010
You attacked our castles,
you brought your men to our citadels.

871
02:20:47,486 --> 02:20:50,720
You despised Byzantium, Osman.

872
02:20:53,066 --> 02:20:57,030
-Now you have lost.
-The time will decide who will lose.

873
02:20:58,446 --> 02:21:02,520
Why are you keeping us alive, why?

874
02:21:08,716 --> 02:21:10,910
So, they are coming.

875
02:21:37,096 --> 02:21:41,650
These Beys are here to save you from me.

876
02:21:43,486 --> 02:21:45,920
Be thankful to them, Osman.

877
02:21:52,486 --> 02:21:55,680
Otherwise, only your dead body
would be able to leave here.

878
02:21:57,576 --> 02:21:59,410
Soldiers.

879
02:22:17,886 --> 02:22:22,120
Lord Zenon, the owner of Lefka.

880
02:22:23,246 --> 02:22:27,480
You listened to me and didn't touch my Bey.

881
02:22:28,766 --> 02:22:34,040
Yakup Bey, son of Germiyanoglu,
if you didn't send your messenger

882
02:22:35,246 --> 02:22:38,160
-Only Osman's dead body would be...
-Never!

883
02:22:39,486 --> 02:22:41,800
Never, Lord.

884
02:22:46,486 --> 02:22:52,040
Osman Bey is one of my most precious Beys.

885
02:22:55,726 --> 02:23:00,680
Would you be alive if he was hurt?

886
02:23:04,846 --> 02:23:09,160
You stopped because you thought what would happen to you.

887
02:23:10,246 --> 02:23:12,040
If an arrow hits one of us,

888
02:23:13,606 --> 02:23:16,760
all of us would bleed, Lord.

889
02:23:30,486 --> 02:23:38,040
Osman Bey, thankfully your captivity
has ended, Thank Allah.

890
02:23:40,486 --> 02:23:42,520
Welcome among us.

891
02:23:49,236 --> 02:23:55,520
White dove has just brought the dark news.

892
02:23:57,286 --> 02:24:04,000
Sultan Mesud passed away.

893
02:24:16,166 --> 02:24:20,040
-May Allah forgive his sins.
-Amin.

894
02:24:21,446 --> 02:24:25,520
Thank you. Long live.

895
02:24:30,406 --> 02:24:35,120
You saved us from the oppressors
may Allah bless you.

896
02:24:36,366 --> 02:24:41,200
Thank you. I owe you my life.

897
02:24:42,286 --> 02:24:45,840
Would I ever leave you behind, Osman Bey?

898
02:24:52,126 --> 02:24:57,800
Your swords will not be sheathed
before you shed each other's blood.

899
02:24:59,926 --> 02:25:01,960
We're beginning now.

900
02:25:07,926 --> 02:25:09,840
From now on

901
02:25:11,086 --> 02:25:15,320
I'm the Sultan of all the Beys in Anatolia.

902
02:25:23,006 --> 02:25:27,280
All of the Beys told that they are behind me.

903
02:25:28,406 --> 02:25:31,920
and that they would walk with me.

904
02:25:46,606 --> 02:25:49,320
Now it's your turn.

905
02:26:02,646 --> 02:26:08,760
Declare your loyalty, kiss my hand, Osman Bey.

906
02:26:29,886 --> 02:26:35,760
We don't want to walk behind
the one that follows the path of The Righteous.

907
02:26:37,366 --> 02:26:39,650
Instead, we want to walk side by side.

908
02:26:56,947 --> 02:27:06,377
Please contact us for any inquiries: turkision@gmail.com